@startuml class-diagram
' Least-connections load balancer: class structure
' Render:  plantuml docs/class-diagram.puml
' Or paste into https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml

title Least-Connections Load Balancer - Class Structure

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
hide empty members

package "com.assignment.loadbalancer" {

  interface PooledLoadBalancer {
    + acquire() : Lease
    + servers() : List<Server>
  }

  class LeastConnectionsBalancer {
    - servers : List<Server>
    - lock : Object
    - cursor : int
    + acquire() : Lease
    + servers() : List<Server>
    - selectLocked(start : int) : Server
    - release(server : Server) : void
  }
  note bottom of LeastConnectionsBalancer
    Scan, capacity check and claim happen
    inside ONE lock: selecting a server and
    then claiming it is check-then-act, and
    atomic counters do not close that window.

    cursor is a plain int, not an atomic:
    it is only ever touched under the lock.
  end note

  class Lease {
    - server : Server
    - onRelease : Runnable
    - released : AtomicBoolean
    + server() : Server
    + isReleased() : boolean
    + close() : void
  }
  note right of Lease
    AutoCloseable, so try-with-resources
    releases even when the body throws.
    close() is idempotent via Compare and Set.

    Releases through a callback rather than
    touching the Server, because counts may
    only change under the balancer's lock.
  end note

  class Server {
    + {static} UNLIMITED : int
    - name : String
    - capacity : int
    - connectionCount : AtomicInteger
    + name() : String
    + capacity() : int
    + connectionCount() : int
    + canAccept() : boolean
    ~ incrementConnections() : void
    ~ decrementConnections() : void
  }
  note left of Server
    Does NOT synchronise itself.
    All mutation happens under the
    balancer's lock. AtomicInteger is
    for safe reads outside the lock,
    not the synchronisation mechanism.
  end note

  class ServerPool <<utility>> {
    + {static} defaultPool() : List<Server>
    + {static} defaultPool(capacity : int) : List<Server>
    + {static} named(names : String...) : List<Server>
    + {static} named(capacity : int, names : String...) : List<Server>
    + {static} defaultPoolWithCapacities(caps : Map) : List<Server>
    + {static} withCapacities(names : List, caps : Map) : List<Server>
  }

  class NoServerAvailableException <<exception>> {
    + NoServerAvailableException(message : String)
  }
  note bottom of NoServerAvailableException
    Unchecked. Transient condition:
    the contract is "retry shortly".
  end note

  class Simulation {
    + {static} MIN_HOLD : Duration
    + {static} MAX_HOLD : Duration
    - balancer : PooledLoadBalancer
    - holdMillis : LongSupplier
    + {static} defaultHold(random : Random) : LongSupplier
    + run(clients : int, requestsPerClient : int, timeout : Duration) : Result
  }
  note right of Simulation
    The random 1 to 10 second hold
    lives here, not in the balancer: a load
    balancer has no say in how long a
    caller's work takes.

    The duration can be injected, so tests drive
    the same code path in milliseconds.
  end note

  class Demo <<entry point>>
}

PooledLoadBalancer <|.. LeastConnectionsBalancer
LeastConnectionsBalancer o--> "1..7*" Server : selects from,\nmutates under lock
LeastConnectionsBalancer ..> Lease : creates with\na release callback
LeastConnectionsBalancer ..> NoServerAvailableException : throws
Lease --> Server : reports
ServerPool ..> Server : builds
Simulation --> PooledLoadBalancer : drives with\nconcurrent clients
Demo ..> Simulation
Demo ..> LeastConnectionsBalancer

@enduml
